/-!
# The generating function of a billiard

Let `χ : ℝ → E` be a parametrization of the boundary of a billiard table in a real inner product
space `E`. A billiard trajectory leaving `χ(s)` along the chord to `χ(t)` and reflecting there is
generated by minus the chord length

`S(s, t) = -‖χ(t) - χ(s)‖`

(`TauCeti.billiardGeneratingFunction`), in the sense of generating functions of the first kind
(`TauCeti.cotangentGeneratingSource`, `TauCeti.cotangentGeneratingTarget`). Write
`u = (χ(t) - χ(s)) / ‖χ(t) - χ(s)‖` for the unit direction of the chord. Then

`∂_s S(s, t) = ⟪u, χ'(s)⟫`, `-∂_t S(s, t) = ⟪u, χ'(t)⟫`

(`TauCeti.fderiv_billiardGeneratingFunction`; the two projections are
`TauCeti.cotangentGeneratingSource_billiardGeneratingFunction` and
`TauCeti.cotangentGeneratingTarget_billiardGeneratingFunction`). For a unit-speed parametrization
these are the tangential components `v` and `w` of the velocity of the trajectory leaving `χ(s)`
and arriving at `χ(t)`; by the law of reflection `w` is also the tangential component of the
velocity leaving `χ(t)`. So the cotangent relation `p = ∂_s S`, `P = -∂_t S` generated by
`S` sends the collision state `(s, v)` to the next collision state `(t, w)`. When the chord does not
lie on the tangent line at `χ(s)`, respectively `χ(t)`, the component `v`, respectively `w`, has
absolute value less than the speed `‖χ'(s)‖`, respectively `‖χ'(t)‖`
(`TauCeti.abs_cotangentGeneratingSource_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply_lt_norm_deriv`,
`TauCeti.abs_cotangentGeneratingTarget_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply_lt_norm_deriv`), so it
lies in `(-1, 1)` for a unit-speed curve
(`TauCeti.abs_cotangentGeneratingSource_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply_lt_one`,
`TauCeti.abs_cotangentGeneratingTarget_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply_lt_one`).

For an `L`-periodic parametrization, `S` is invariant under translating both arguments by `L`
(`TauCeti.billiardGeneratingFunction_add_period`), and the chord from `χ(t)` to `χ(s + L)` has the
same length (`TauCeti.billiardGeneratingFunction_swap_add_period`). The function is smooth wherever
the chord is nondegenerate, `χ(t) ≠ χ(s)` (`TauCeti.contDiffAt_billiardGeneratingFunction`). For
the boundary of a table this excludes the diagonal `t = s` and its translates `t = s + kL`, and
the natural domain of `S` is the strip `s < t < s + L`.

The mixed derivative is
`∂_t ∂_s S = (‖D‖² ⟪χ'(s), χ'(t)⟫ - ⟪D, χ'(s)⟫ ⟪D, χ'(t)⟫) / ‖D‖³` with `D = χ(t) - χ(s)`
(`TauCeti.cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction_apply_apply`). In the plane this is
`ω(D, χ'(s)) ω(D, χ'(t)) / ‖D‖³` for the area form `ω` of either orientation
(`TauCeti.cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction_apply_apply_eq_areaForm`). Since
`ω(D, v) = ‖D‖ ‖v‖ sin θ` for the oriented angle `θ` from `D` to `v`, this is
`‖χ'(s)‖ ‖χ'(t)‖ sin θ_s sin θ_t / ‖D‖` for the oriented angles `θ_s`, `θ_t` from the chord to
`χ'(s)`, `χ'(t)`. On a convex table these have opposite signs, so `∂_t ∂_s S` is minus the product
of the sines of the interior angles `α, β ∈ (0, π)` between the chord and the curve at its two
ends, scaled by the speeds and divided by `‖D‖`.

For a strictly convex table the twist condition `∂_t ∂_s S < 0` holds on the whole domain
`s < t < s + L` (`TauCeti.cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction_apply_apply_neg`): if
no chord `χ(s) χ(t)` with `s < t < s + L` lies on the tangent line at `χ(s)`, then
`F(s, t) = ω(χ'(s), χ(t) - χ(s))` vanishes nowhere on this connected domain
(`Orientation.areaForm_ne_zero_iff`), so it has constant sign, and the two area forms are
`ω(D, χ'(s)) = -F(s, t)` and `ω(D, χ'(t)) = F(t, s + L)`. This sign argument needs neither an
orientation of the table nor a unit-speed condition. The mixed Hessian is invertible at every
chord lying on neither of the tangent lines at its ends
(`TauCeti.isInvertible_cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction`), in particular on the
domain of a strictly convex table, so near such a chord the relation generated by `S` is the graph
of a local canonical transformation (`TauCeti.cotangentGeneratedMap`). In terms of the tangential
component `v = ∂_s S(s, t)`, the twist condition says that `v` has negative derivative in `t` for
fixed `s`.

## References

* A. Cannas da Silva, *Lectures on Symplectic Geometry*, Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1764,
  Springer, 2001, Section 5.2.
* S. Tabachnikov, *Geometry and Billiards*, Student Mathematical Library 30, American Mathematical
  Society, 2005, Chapter 3.
-/

public section

open ContinuousLinearMap Set
open scoped RealInnerProductSpace

namespace TauCeti

variable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] {χ : ℝ → E}

/-- The **generating function of the billiard** in the curve `χ`: minus the length of the chord
from `χ s` to `χ t`, `S(s, t) = -‖χ t - χ s‖`. -/
def billiardGeneratingFunction (χ : ℝ → E) (x : ℝ × ℝ) : ℝ :=
  -‖χ x.2 - χ x.1‖

theorem billiardGeneratingFunction_def (χ : ℝ → E) (x : ℝ × ℝ) :
    billiardGeneratingFunction χ x = -‖χ x.2 - χ x.1‖ :=
  (rfl)

theorem billiardGeneratingFunction_apply (χ : ℝ → E) (s t : ℝ) :
    billiardGeneratingFunction χ (s, t) = -‖χ t - χ s‖ :=
  (rfl)

/-- The degenerate chord from a point to itself has length zero. -/
@[simp]
theorem billiardGeneratingFunction_self (χ : ℝ → E) (s : ℝ) :
    billiardGeneratingFunction χ (s, s) = 0 := by
  simp [billiardGeneratingFunction_apply]

/-- The chord from `χ t` to `χ s` has the same length as the chord from `χ s` to `χ t`. -/
theorem billiardGeneratingFunction_swap (χ : ℝ → E) (x : ℝ × ℝ) :
    billiardGeneratingFunction χ x.swap = billiardGeneratingFunction χ x := by
  simp [billiardGeneratingFunction_def, norm_sub_rev]

/-! ### Periodicity -/

/-- For an `L`-periodic curve, the billiard generating function is invariant under translating
both arguments by `L`. -/
theorem billiardGeneratingFunction_add_period {L : ℝ} (hχ : Function.Periodic χ L) (s t : ℝ) :
    billiardGeneratingFunction χ (s + L, t + L) = billiardGeneratingFunction χ (s, t) := by
  simp [billiardGeneratingFunction_apply, hχ s, hχ t]

/-- For an `L`-periodic curve, the chord from `χ t` to `χ (s + L)` is the chord from `χ s` to `χ t`
traversed backwards. -/
theorem billiardGeneratingFunction_swap_add_period {L : ℝ} (hχ : Function.Periodic χ L)
    (s t : ℝ) :
    billiardGeneratingFunction χ (t, s + L) = billiardGeneratingFunction χ (s, t) := by
  simp [billiardGeneratingFunction_apply, hχ s, norm_sub_rev]

/-! ### Smoothness and first derivatives -/

variable [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]

/-- The billiard generating function is `C^n` at every nondegenerate chord of a `C^n` curve. -/
theorem contDiffAt_billiardGeneratingFunction {n : WithTop ℕ∞} {s t : ℝ}
    (hs : ContDiffAt ℝ n χ s) (ht : ContDiffAt ℝ n χ t) (hst : χ t ≠ χ s) :
    ContDiffAt ℝ n (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t) :=
  (((ht.comp (s, t) contDiffAt_snd).sub (hs.comp (s, t) contDiffAt_fst)).norm ℝ
    (sub_ne_zero.2 hst)).neg

/-- **The derivative of the billiard generating function.** At a nondegenerate chord `D = χ t - χ s`
of a curve with velocities `a` at `s` and `b` at `t`, the derivative of `S` is
`(δs, δt) ↦ ‖D‖⁻¹ (⟪D, a⟫ δs - ⟪D, b⟫ δt)`. -/
theorem hasFDerivAt_billiardGeneratingFunction {s t : ℝ} {a b : E} (hs : HasDerivAt χ a s)
    (ht : HasDerivAt χ b t) (hst : χ t ≠ χ s) :
    HasFDerivAt (billiardGeneratingFunction χ)
      (‖χ t - χ s‖⁻¹ • (⟪χ t - χ s, a⟫ • fst ℝ ℝ ℝ - ⟪χ t - χ s, b⟫ • snd ℝ ℝ ℝ)) (s, t) := by
  have hD : HasFDerivAt (fun x : ℝ × ℝ ↦ χ x.2 - χ x.1)
      ((smulRight (1 : ℝ →L[ℝ] ℝ) b).comp (snd ℝ ℝ ℝ) -
        (smulRight (1 : ℝ →L[ℝ] ℝ) a).comp (fst ℝ ℝ ℝ)) (s, t) :=
    (ht.hasFDerivAt.comp (s, t) hasFDerivAt_snd).sub (hs.hasFDerivAt.comp (s, t) hasFDerivAt_fst)
  have h := ((hasFDerivAt_norm_of_ne (sub_ne_zero.2 hst)).comp (s, t) hD).neg
  refine h.congr_fderiv (ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun x ↦ ?_)
  simp [inner_sub_left]
  ring

/-- The derivative of the billiard generating function at a nondegenerate chord
`D = χ t - χ s`: `(δs, δt) ↦ ‖D‖⁻¹ (⟪D, χ'(s)⟫ δs - ⟪D, χ'(t)⟫ δt)`. -/
theorem fderiv_billiardGeneratingFunction {s t : ℝ} (hs : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ s)
    (ht : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ t) (hst : χ t ≠ χ s) :
    fderiv ℝ (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t) =
      ‖χ t - χ s‖⁻¹ • (⟪χ t - χ s, deriv χ s⟫ • fst ℝ ℝ ℝ - ⟪χ t - χ s, deriv χ t⟫ • snd ℝ ℝ ℝ) :=
  (hasFDerivAt_billiardGeneratingFunction hs.hasDerivAt ht.hasDerivAt hst).fderiv

/-- The source covector of the relation generated by the billiard generating function: at a
nondegenerate chord, `∂_s S(s, t) δs = δs ⟪u, χ'(s)⟫` for the unit direction `u` of the chord. -/
theorem cotangentGeneratingSource_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply {s t : ℝ}
    (hs : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ s) (ht : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ t) (hst : χ t ≠ χ s) (r : ℝ) :
    (cotangentGeneratingSource (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t)).2 r =
      r * ⟪‖χ t - χ s‖⁻¹ • (χ t - χ s), deriv χ s⟫ := by
  rw [cotangentGeneratingSource_snd_apply, fderiv_billiardGeneratingFunction hs ht hst]
  simp [real_inner_smul_left]
  ring

/-- The target covector of the relation generated by the billiard generating function: at a
nondegenerate chord, `-∂_t S(s, t) δt = δt ⟪u, χ'(t)⟫` for the unit direction `u` of the
chord. -/
theorem cotangentGeneratingTarget_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply {s t : ℝ}
    (hs : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ s) (ht : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ t) (hst : χ t ≠ χ s) (r : ℝ) :
    (cotangentGeneratingTarget (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t)).2 r =
      r * ⟪‖χ t - χ s‖⁻¹ • (χ t - χ s), deriv χ t⟫ := by
  rw [cotangentGeneratingTarget_snd_apply, fderiv_billiardGeneratingFunction hs ht hst]
  simp [real_inner_smul_left]
  ring

/-- The source projection of the relation generated by the billiard generating function sends a
nondegenerate chord `(s, t)` to `(s, ⟪u, χ'(s)⟫)` for the unit direction `u` of the chord. For a
unit-speed curve, `⟪u, χ'(s)⟫` is the tangential component of the velocity leaving `χ s` along
the chord. -/
theorem cotangentGeneratingSource_billiardGeneratingFunction {s t : ℝ}
    (hs : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ s) (ht : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ t) (hst : χ t ≠ χ s) :
    cotangentGeneratingSource (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t) =
      (s, toSpanSingleton ℝ ⟪‖χ t - χ s‖⁻¹ • (χ t - χ s), deriv χ s⟫) :=
  Prod.ext (cotangentGeneratingSource_fst _ _) <| ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun r ↦ by
    rw [cotangentGeneratingSource_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply hs ht hst,
      toSpanSingleton_apply, smul_eq_mul]

/-- The target projection of the relation generated by the billiard generating function sends a
nondegenerate chord `(s, t)` to `(t, ⟪u, χ'(t)⟫)` for the unit direction `u` of the chord. For a
unit-speed curve, `⟪u, χ'(t)⟫` is the tangential component of the velocity arriving at `χ t`
along the chord. -/
theorem cotangentGeneratingTarget_billiardGeneratingFunction {s t : ℝ}
    (hs : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ s) (ht : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ t) (hst : χ t ≠ χ s) :
    cotangentGeneratingTarget (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t) =
      (t, toSpanSingleton ℝ ⟪‖χ t - χ s‖⁻¹ • (χ t - χ s), deriv χ t⟫) :=
  Prod.ext (cotangentGeneratingTarget_fst _ _) <| ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun r ↦ by
    rw [cotangentGeneratingTarget_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply hs ht hst,
      toSpanSingleton_apply, smul_eq_mul]

/-- The tangential component `∂_s S(s, t)` of a chord which does not lie on the tangent line at
`χ s` has absolute value less than the speed `‖χ'(s)‖`. -/
theorem abs_cotangentGeneratingSource_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply_lt_norm_deriv
    {s t : ℝ} (hs : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ s) (ht : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ t) (hs0 : deriv χ s ≠ 0)
    (htan : ∀ c : ℝ, χ t ≠ χ s + c • deriv χ s) :
    |(cotangentGeneratingSource (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t)).2 1| < ‖deriv χ s‖ := by
  have hst : χ t ≠ χ s := by simpa using htan 0
  rw [cotangentGeneratingSource_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply hs ht hst, one_mul,
    real_inner_smul_left, abs_mul, abs_inv, abs_norm,
    inv_mul_lt_iff₀ (norm_pos_iff.2 (sub_ne_zero.2 hst)), real_inner_comm, mul_comm]
  exact (abs_real_inner_lt_norm_mul_norm_iff hs0).2 fun c hc ↦
    htan c (by rw [← hc, add_sub_cancel])

/-- The tangential component `-∂_t S(s, t)` of a chord which does not lie on the tangent line at
`χ t` has absolute value less than the speed `‖χ'(t)‖`. -/
theorem abs_cotangentGeneratingTarget_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply_lt_norm_deriv
    {s t : ℝ} (hs : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ s) (ht : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ t) (ht0 : deriv χ t ≠ 0)
    (htan : ∀ c : ℝ, χ s ≠ χ t + c • deriv χ t) :
    |(cotangentGeneratingTarget (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t)).2 1| < ‖deriv χ t‖ := by
  -- Reversing the chord negates the unit direction, so this is the bound at the chord `(t, s)`.
  have hts : χ s ≠ χ t := by simpa using htan 0
  have h :=
    abs_cotangentGeneratingSource_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply_lt_norm_deriv ht hs ht0 htan
  rwa [cotangentGeneratingSource_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply ht hs hts, ← neg_sub,
    norm_neg, smul_neg, inner_neg_left, mul_neg, abs_neg,
    ← cotangentGeneratingTarget_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply hs ht hts.symm] at h

/-- For a unit-speed curve, the tangential component `∂_s S(s, t)` of a chord which does not lie on
the tangent line at `χ s` is in `(-1, 1)`. -/
theorem abs_cotangentGeneratingSource_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply_lt_one {s t : ℝ}
    (hs : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ s) (ht : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ t) (hs1 : ‖deriv χ s‖ = 1)
    (htan : ∀ c : ℝ, χ t ≠ χ s + c • deriv χ s) :
    |(cotangentGeneratingSource (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t)).2 1| < 1 :=
  hs1 ▸ abs_cotangentGeneratingSource_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply_lt_norm_deriv hs ht
    (norm_ne_zero_iff.1 (by simp [hs1])) htan

/-- For a unit-speed curve, the tangential component `-∂_t S(s, t)` of a chord which does not lie
on the tangent line at `χ t` is in `(-1, 1)`. -/
theorem abs_cotangentGeneratingTarget_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply_lt_one {s t : ℝ}
    (hs : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ s) (ht : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ t) (ht1 : ‖deriv χ t‖ = 1)
    (htan : ∀ c : ℝ, χ s ≠ χ t + c • deriv χ t) :
    |(cotangentGeneratingTarget (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t)).2 1| < 1 :=
  ht1 ▸ abs_cotangentGeneratingTarget_billiardGeneratingFunction_snd_apply_lt_norm_deriv hs ht
    (norm_ne_zero_iff.1 (by simp [ht1])) htan

/-! ### The mixed derivative -/

/-- A mixed Hessian on `ℝ × ℝ` is determined by its value at `1 1`. -/
private theorem cotangentMixedHessian_apply_apply_eq_mul (S : ℝ × ℝ → ℝ) (x : ℝ × ℝ)
    (b a : ℝ) :
    cotangentMixedHessian S x b a = b * a * cotangentMixedHessian S x 1 1 := by
  have h := congr($((cotangentMixedHessian S x).map_smul b 1) a)
  have h' := (cotangentMixedHessian S x 1).map_smul a 1
  simp only [smul_eq_mul, mul_one, smul_apply] at h h'
  rw [h, h']
  ring

/-- The mixed derivative at `1 1`, from which `cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction`
follows by linearity. -/
private theorem cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction_one_one {s t : ℝ}
    (hs : ContDiffAt ℝ 2 χ s) (ht : ContDiffAt ℝ 2 χ t) (hst : χ t ≠ χ s) :
    cotangentMixedHessian (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t) 1 1 =
      (‖χ t - χ s‖ ^ 2 * ⟪deriv χ s, deriv χ t⟫ -
        ⟪χ t - χ s, deriv χ s⟫ * ⟪χ t - χ s, deriv χ t⟫) / ‖χ t - χ s‖ ^ 3 := by
  set S := billiardGeneratingFunction χ
  set a := deriv χ s
  set D : ℝ → E := fun t' ↦ χ t' - χ s
  have hD : D t ≠ 0 := sub_ne_zero.2 hst
  have hds : DifferentiableAt ℝ χ s := hs.differentiableAt (by norm_num)
  have hdt : HasDerivAt χ (deriv χ t) t := (ht.differentiableAt (by norm_num)).hasDerivAt
  -- The mixed derivative is the derivative in `t` of the partial derivative `∂_s S(s, t)`.
  have h₁ : HasDerivAt (fun t' ↦ fderiv ℝ S (s, t') (1, 0))
      (cotangentMixedHessian S (s, t) 1 1) t := by
    rw [cotangentMixedHessian_apply_apply]
    exact hasDerivAt_fderiv_apply_snd
      ((contDiffAt_billiardGeneratingFunction hs ht hst).hasFDerivAt_fderiv le_rfl).differentiableAt
      (1, 0)
  -- Near `t` the function `t' ↦ ∂_s S(s, t')` is `⟪D t', a⟫ * ‖D t'‖⁻¹`.
  have hev : (fun t' ↦ fderiv ℝ S (s, t') (1, 0)) =ᶠ[nhds t]
      fun t' ↦ ⟪D t', a⟫ * ‖D t'‖⁻¹ := by
    have hcont : ContinuousAt D t := (hdt.continuousAt).sub continuousAt_const
    filter_upwards [hcont.eventually_ne hD, ht.eventually (by simp)] with t' ht' ht'2
    rw [fderiv_billiardGeneratingFunction hds (ht'2.differentiableAt (by norm_num))
      (sub_ne_zero.1 ht')]
    simp [D, a, mul_comm]
  have hDt : HasDerivAt D (deriv χ t) t := by simpa [D] using hdt.sub_const (χ s)
  have hnorm : HasDerivAt (fun t' ↦ ‖D t'‖) (‖D t‖⁻¹ * ⟪D t, deriv χ t⟫) t := by
    have h := (hasFDerivAt_norm_of_ne hD).comp_hasDerivAt t hDt
    simp only [Function.comp_def, smul_apply, innerSL_apply_apply, smul_eq_mul] at h
    exact h
  have h₂ : HasDerivAt (fun t' ↦ ⟪D t', a⟫ * ‖D t'‖⁻¹)
      (⟪deriv χ t, a⟫ * ‖D t‖⁻¹ +
        ⟪D t, a⟫ * (-(‖D t‖⁻¹ * ⟪D t, deriv χ t⟫) / ‖D t‖ ^ 2)) t := by
    have hinner : HasDerivAt (fun t' ↦ ⟪D t', a⟫) ⟪deriv χ t, a⟫ t := by
      simpa using HasDerivAt.inner ℝ hDt (hasDerivAt_const t a)
    exact hinner.mul (hnorm.inv (norm_ne_zero_iff.2 hD))
  rw [(h₁.congr_of_eventuallyEq hev.symm).unique h₂]
  have hn : ‖D t‖ ≠ 0 := norm_ne_zero_iff.2 hD
  simp only [D] at hn ⊢
  rw [real_inner_comm (deriv χ t) a]
  field_simp
  ring

/-- **The mixed derivative of the billiard generating function.** At a nondegenerate chord
`D = χ t - χ s` of a `C²` curve, `∂_t ∂_s S(s, t) (δt, δs) =
δt δs (‖D‖² ⟪χ'(s), χ'(t)⟫ - ⟪D, χ'(s)⟫ ⟪D, χ'(t)⟫) / ‖D‖³`. -/
theorem cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction_apply_apply {s t : ℝ}
    (hs : ContDiffAt ℝ 2 χ s) (ht : ContDiffAt ℝ 2 χ t) (hst : χ t ≠ χ s) (b a : ℝ) :
    cotangentMixedHessian (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t) b a =
      b * a * (‖χ t - χ s‖ ^ 2 * ⟪deriv χ s, deriv χ t⟫ -
        ⟪χ t - χ s, deriv χ s⟫ * ⟪χ t - χ s, deriv χ t⟫) / ‖χ t - χ s‖ ^ 3 := by
  rw [cotangentMixedHessian_apply_apply_eq_mul,
    cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction_one_one hs ht hst, mul_div_assoc]

/-- **The mixed derivative of a planar billiard generating function.** In an oriented plane with
area form `ω`, at a nondegenerate chord `D = χ t - χ s` of a `C²` curve,
`∂_t ∂_s S(s, t) (δt, δs) = δt δs ω(D, χ'(s)) ω(D, χ'(t)) / ‖D‖³`. -/
theorem cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction_apply_apply_eq_areaForm
    [Fact (Module.finrank ℝ E = 2)] (o : Orientation ℝ E (Fin 2)) {s t : ℝ}
    (hs : ContDiffAt ℝ 2 χ s) (ht : ContDiffAt ℝ 2 χ t) (hst : χ t ≠ χ s) (b a : ℝ) :
    cotangentMixedHessian (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t) b a =
      b * a * (o.areaForm (χ t - χ s) (deriv χ s) * o.areaForm (χ t - χ s) (deriv χ t)) /
        ‖χ t - χ s‖ ^ 3 := by
  rw [cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction_apply_apply hs ht hst,
    ← o.inner_mul_inner_add_areaForm_mul_areaForm]
  ring_nf

/-- **The twist condition for a strictly convex billiard.** Let `χ` be a `C²`, `L`-periodic curve
in a two-dimensional real inner product space, with nonvanishing velocity, such that for
`s < t < s + L` the point `χ t` does not lie on the tangent line `{χ s + c χ'(s)}`. Then the
billiard generating function satisfies `∂_t ∂_s S(s, t) < 0` for all `s < t < s + L`.

The hypothesis holds for an arclength parametrization of the boundary of a strictly convex table,
injective on `[0, L)` and meeting each tangent line only at the point of tangency. -/
theorem cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction_apply_apply_neg
    [Fact (Module.finrank ℝ E = 2)] {L : ℝ} (hχ : ContDiff ℝ 2 χ) (hper : Function.Periodic χ L)
    (hχ' : ∀ s, deriv χ s ≠ 0)
    (htan : ∀ s t, s < t → t < s + L → ∀ c : ℝ, χ t ≠ χ s + c • deriv χ s) {s t : ℝ}
    (hst : s < t) (hts : t < s + L) :
    cotangentMixedHessian (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t) 1 1 < 0 := by
  have : FiniteDimensional ℝ E := .of_fact_finrank_eq_two
  let o : Orientation ℝ E (Fin 2) := (Module.finBasisOfFinrankEq ℝ E Fact.out).orientation
  set U : Set (ℝ × ℝ) := {x | x.1 < x.2 ∧ x.2 < x.1 + L}
  set F : ℝ × ℝ → ℝ := fun x ↦ o.areaForm (deriv χ x.1) (χ x.2 - χ x.1)
  have hU : IsPreconnected U := by
    -- `U` is the intersection of the open half-planes `s - t < 0` and `t - s < L`.
    convert ((convex_halfSpace_lt (LinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ - LinearMap.snd ℝ ℝ ℝ).isLinear 0).inter
      (convex_halfSpace_lt (LinearMap.snd ℝ ℝ ℝ - LinearMap.fst ℝ ℝ ℝ).isLinear L)).isPreconnected
      using 1
    ext x
    simp [U, sub_lt_iff_lt_add']
  have hF : ContinuousOn F U := by
    have hcont : Continuous fun x : ℝ × ℝ ↦
        ⟪o.rightAngleRotation (deriv χ x.1), χ x.2 - χ x.1⟫ :=
      (o.rightAngleRotation.continuous.comp ((hχ.continuous_deriv (by norm_num)).comp
        continuous_fst)).inner ((hχ.continuous.comp continuous_snd).sub
          (hχ.continuous.comp continuous_fst))
    simpa [F, o.inner_rightAngleRotation_left] using hcont.continuousOn
  have hF0 : ∀ x ∈ U, F x ≠ 0 := fun x hx ↦
    (o.areaForm_ne_zero_iff (hχ' x.1)).2 fun c hc ↦
      htan x.1 x.2 hx.1 hx.2 c (by rw [← hc, add_sub_cancel])
  have hmem₁ : (s, t) ∈ U := ⟨hst, hts⟩
  have hmem₂ : (t, s + L) ∈ U := ⟨hts, by linarith⟩
  -- `F(s, t)` and `F(t, s + L)` have the same sign, and the mixed derivative is
  -- `-F(s, t) F(t, s + L) / ‖D‖³`.
  have hsign := hU.sign_eq_of_continuousOn hF hF0 hmem₁ hmem₂
  have hpos : 0 < F (s, t) * F (t, s + L) := by
    rcases (hF0 _ hmem₁).lt_or_gt with h | h <;>
      rcases (hF0 _ hmem₂).lt_or_gt with h' | h' <;>
      simp_all [sign_neg, sign_pos, mul_pos_of_neg_of_neg]
  have hD : χ t ≠ χ s := by simpa using htan s t hst hts 0
  rw [cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction_apply_apply_eq_areaForm o
    (hχ.contDiffAt) (hχ.contDiffAt) hD, one_mul, one_mul]
  have h₁ : o.areaForm (χ t - χ s) (deriv χ s) = -F (s, t) := o.areaForm_swap _ _
  have h₂ : o.areaForm (χ t - χ s) (deriv χ t) = F (t, s + L) := by
    simp only [F, hper s]
    rw [o.areaForm_swap, ← map_neg, neg_sub]
  rw [h₁, h₂, neg_mul]
  exact div_neg_of_neg_of_pos (neg_neg_of_pos hpos)
    (pow_pos (norm_pos_iff.2 (sub_ne_zero.2 hD)) 3)

/-- **The billiard generating function is nondegenerate.** In a two-dimensional real inner product
space, at a chord `(s, t)` of a curve which is `C²` near `s` and `t`, with nonzero velocities there,
such that the chord lies neither on the tangent line at `χ s` nor on the tangent line at `χ t`, the
mixed Hessian of the billiard generating function is invertible. Under the hypotheses of
`TauCeti.cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction_apply_apply_neg` this holds at every
`(s, t)` with `s < t < s + L`, applying the tangent-line hypothesis also to the chord
`(t, s + L)`. -/
theorem isInvertible_cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction
    [Fact (Module.finrank ℝ E = 2)] {s t : ℝ} (hs : ContDiffAt ℝ 2 χ s) (ht : ContDiffAt ℝ 2 χ t)
    (hs0 : deriv χ s ≠ 0) (ht0 : deriv χ t ≠ 0) (htan_s : ∀ c : ℝ, χ t ≠ χ s + c • deriv χ s)
    (htan_t : ∀ c : ℝ, χ s ≠ χ t + c • deriv χ t) :
    (cotangentMixedHessian (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t)).IsInvertible := by
  have : FiniteDimensional ℝ E := .of_fact_finrank_eq_two
  let o : Orientation ℝ E (Fin 2) := (Module.finBasisOfFinrankEq ℝ E Fact.out).orientation
  have hst : χ t ≠ χ s := by simpa using htan_s 0
  have hD : ‖χ t - χ s‖ ≠ 0 := norm_ne_zero_iff.2 (sub_ne_zero.2 hst)
  -- Both area forms are nonzero, since the chord is not a multiple of either velocity.
  have hωs : o.areaForm (χ t - χ s) (deriv χ s) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [o.areaForm_swap, neg_ne_zero, o.areaForm_ne_zero_iff hs0]
    exact fun c hc ↦ htan_s c (by rw [← hc, add_sub_cancel])
  have hωt : o.areaForm (χ t - χ s) (deriv χ t) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [← neg_sub, map_neg, LinearMap.neg_apply, neg_ne_zero, o.areaForm_swap, neg_ne_zero,
      o.areaForm_ne_zero_iff ht0]
    exact fun c hc ↦ htan_t c (by rw [← hc, add_sub_cancel])
  have hm : cotangentMixedHessian (billiardGeneratingFunction χ) (s, t) 1 1 ≠ 0 := by
    rw [cotangentMixedHessian_billiardGeneratingFunction_apply_apply_eq_areaForm o hs ht hst,
      mul_one, one_mul]
    exact div_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero hωs hωt) (pow_ne_zero 3 hD)
  refine ContinuousLinearMap.isInvertible_of_injective fun b b' h ↦ ?_
  have h1 := congr($h 1)
  rw [cotangentMixedHessian_apply_apply_eq_mul, cotangentMixedHessian_apply_apply_eq_mul _ _ b',
    mul_one, mul_one] at h1
  exact mul_right_cancel₀ hm h1

end TauCeti
